+From 44031c5a5811435fffa4daa1d5ead9b9c31486f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: max994-dev <bmax994@outlook.com>
+Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:57:31 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 3/6] OneTrust state options: match on full name or code
+ instead of the raw profile value
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+- lib/broker_helpers.py: add select_onetrust_state(). OneTrust DSAR forms
+  label their <vt-option> entries with the FULL state name ("Texas"), but 13
+  scripts interpolated dataRow["State"] straight into the selector, so a
+  "TX" profile looked for an option labelled "Tx" and raised
+  ElementNotFoundError — 82 failures in the 2026-09-21..24 run. The helper
+  tries the full name, the raw value and the upper-case code against both
+  aria-label and text(), and raises naming the real cause when none match.
+
+- sites/datatrustcom.py had the worse variant: a raw usaStateDictionary
+  lookup that KeyErrors on "TX", with an else-branch that clicked
+  vt-option[0] — filing the deletion request under whatever state happened
+  to be first in the list rather than failing. Now it raises.
+
+- lib/broker_helpers.py: the *arrests.org name covers two different
+  platforms. Only some (indianaarrests.org) run the WPForms portal; the rest
+  (dcarrests.org, marylandarrests.org, the Carolinas, Idaho) have no opt-out
+  portal at all and expose only a Contact Form 7 at /contact-form. Submit a
+  CCPA/CPRA deletion request there before declaring "no form", which is the
+  documented route for those sites.
+
+- sites/ (15 scripts): call the helper instead of interpolating the state.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
