@@ -0,0 +1,378 @@
+From 62bbb410e7e3238ae9b79a3bd1bda801edf89e32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: max994-dev <bmax994@outlook.com>
+Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:19:41 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Pipeline: retry transient DOM errors, quarantine dead
+ brokers, log successes, DB retry, scan empty-name
+
+From the 24 Sep - 2 Oct daily logs (~240k lines):
+
+- ~440 crashes/day were DrissionPage element-timing errors on brokers that
+  succeed 60-70% of the time (acbjcom 101 ok / 58 crash, accudatacom 134/57,
+  archivescom 130/61, ...). Each crash cost a day: requeued, retried tomorrow.
+  A transient DOM error now gets one immediate retry in a fresh browser
+  (REMOVAL_TRANSIENT_RETRIES, default 1) before it counts as a crash.
+- advancedbackgroundcheckscom has never succeeded and still got 57 attempts in
+  nine days. Brokers with >= DEAD_DOMAIN_FAILS failures and no success in 7 days
+  are held back from bulk selection; their daily probe row still runs so a
+  repaired script is noticed within a day.
+- Successes were never logged (_set_step only logged when a reason was given),
+  so the logs could not show a success rate. Every transition is logged now.
+- The managed DB drops connections occasionally ('Lost connection', connect
+  timeouts): a tick died on the first hiccup. _db_connect() retries 3x.
+- Scan scripts start with Name.split()[0]; an account with no name crashed as
+  IndexError and was recorded as a broken broker (41 times). It is now
+  IncompletePII -> step 5 (needs customer data) in both scan loops.
+- A None proxy extension crashed browser setup instead of running without one.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
